From 00e7b637b5037a7ed5a60ba96bd96ca8672a3503 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jolyon Brown <jolyon@limilo.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:12:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Far spaces: groups go on into the blocks that follow

A procedure-level driver lowers far accesses block by block, in
depth-first order. A group still open at the end of a block goes on
into a later block that uses it. A block takes a group over when every
block leading into it passes on the same translation in the same slot,
and all of them come before it, so never over a loop's way back.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
